  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nCome early Friday, there is strong guidance agreement that our \narea will remain under a dry west-northwest zonal flow, \ncontinuing a near- normal temperature trend. A shortwave trough \nwill dig across the area from off the northwest coast Saturday \nthrough Sunday. This pattern will be mostly dry over our area, \nfavoring some light isolated showers over the northernmost \nmountain areas of our CWA. A cooling trend from this pattern \nwill drop daytime temperatures 5 to 10 degrees below normal over\nthe weekend. Come Monday through Tuesday, there is some \nguidance disagreement over whether the area will stay under a \nwest-northwest zonal flow or be under another dry shortwave \ntrough. For now, dry conditions and a warming trend to normal \ntemperatures are expected early next week.",
